+### 2. Added incremental stacking / progression guidance (`## ⚡ PROGRESSION / INCREMENTAL STACKING`)
+- Instructs the task agent to make **exactly ONE major structural addition per generation** (e.g., LPSR this gen, restart next gen, local search after that).
+- Provides concrete mechanisms to stack on top of existing SHADE:
+  - L-SHADE's Linear Population Size Reduction (LPSR)
+  - Restart when diversity collapses
+  - Local search / hill-climbing
+  - Opposition-based learning (OBL)
+  - Ensemble / multi-operator DE
+- This prevents the "change everything at once" failure mode and ensures each generation's contribution can be isolated.
+
+### 3. Added weak-problem targeting section (`## 🎯 TARGET WEAK PROBLEMS`)
+- Instructs the task agent to read the progress info and generate.log to identify which BBOB functions are consistently underperforming (f14, f7, f15, f10 in recent runs).
+- Gives concrete strategies for weak functions (typically multimodal / ill-conditioned):
+  - Increase diversity (larger initial population, dither)
+  - Add restart
+  - Consider CMA-ES for ill-conditioned problems
+  - More aggressive F/CR adaptation (L-SHADE or jDE)
+
+## Eariler changes (kept for reference):
